// The studio's tool: the lens on a subject package (`wrela tool studio`). The lens is the
// `studio` package (wrela, generic over any surface); its program is studio/glue's (an export,
// and a typed command, for each action) around a module `subject` this tool writes for the
// subject's `subject()`. The tool builds that program with the subject's literals lifted,
// through the toolchain service, serves it to Chrome on 127.0.0.1, and runs its actions
// headless on the native host.
//
// ```text
// wrela tool studio -- <package-dir> [serve [--port N] | build | run <script> | look
//     | beside <photo> | variants <package-dir>... | sweep <literal> <value>...
//     | <action> [args...]] [--png FILE] [--view F] [--size WxH] [--reference PNG] [--debug]
// ```
//
// Each path is from the workspace's directory (the tool's root `ws`). The lens's program, its
// probe and its build go in `build/studio/<package-dir>/` (the root `out`), never beside the
// subject's sources; the subject is read as a dependency of the program, from its own directory.
//
// **A subject** is a package with a module `subject.wrela` with `pub fn subject()`, which
// returns a `Surface`, or a `Field<C>` for its channels: the probe shows each of the channels'
// public float fields, and the colour mode shows their first `r`, `g`, `b` floats (the albedo)
// where the channels' type is the subject's own or std's. A module `spec` with `pub fn spec<C:
// Checks>(c: mut C)` is its spec (language.md §23.6), and a module `blueprint` with any of `pub
// fn side()`, `front()` and `top()` is its blueprint (§23.7). A package whose module `lens` has
// `pub fn map()` and `pub fn preview()` is a floor, which the map lens (studio/maplens) shows:
// the map's literals alone are lifted. A game whose module `lens` has `pub fn course()` (its
// chains' corners, its ground's lines and its water's boxes) and `pub fn run()` (its player's
// path) is a course, which the course lens (studio/courselens) shows, its player running over
// it: its `course.wrela`'s literals alone are lifted, and a drag moves a corner by them
// (`corners`, `click x y`, `move x0 y0 x1 y1`, `write`, `zoom x y half`).
//
// **Every action is an export and a command,** and answers with one line of JSON.
// `<action> [args...]` runs one action headless on the native host and prints its lines;
// `--png` saves the screen after it, at `--size` (896x896 unless given: under 900 pixels wide,
// the views fill the screen). An action whose answer needs only the lens's state on the CPU
// (`literals`, `parts`, `probe`, `ray`, `measure`, `spec`, `view`, `zoom`, `mode`, `set`,
// `choose`, `choose_none`) runs without the GPU unless a PNG is asked for. `run <script>` runs
// a session, one command a line as a person types it into the lens, and `png <file>` saves the
// screen (its path from the script's directory); the same session typed into Chrome gives the
// same answers, files and frames.
//
// | Action | What it does |
// |---|---|
// | `view f` | Shows a facing (side, front, three-quarter or top, by name or 0 to 3) or the contact sheet (4) |
// | `mode m p` | Sets the shading: shaded, parts, tint, isolate, silhouette or colour, with a part |
// | `zoom c h` | Frames a close-up `2 h` metres across at `c`, with a 1 cm grid under 30 cm; `zoom off` undoes it |
// | `parts` | Lists the parts' names |
// | `probe x y z` | Gives the distance, gradient, part and channels at a point |
// | `ray o d` | Gives the first hit and its part |
// | `measure a b` | Measures between two points, as a tape measure does |
// | `project p` | Gives a point's pixel in each view |
// | `diagnose c r` | Pieces, and pieces if thin parts' cells join; bounds; the largest gradient and the five places where it is worst, each with its part; the Lipschitz bound, stated and derived |
// | `describe` | Each part's volume, box and contacts, and the whole subject's box, volume, mass, pieces, lowest point and asymmetry |
// | `click x y` | The part under a pixel, and every literal that moves the surface there, ranked by the distance's derivative by it, with its source line |
// | `literals` | Lists the lifted literals |
// | `set i v` | Sets a new value; the views show it at the next frame |
// | `write` | Writes every changed value through `wrela edit` |
// | `move a b` | Drags: the point on the surface at `a` moves to `b`, by the literals named after it (or those that move it most), with other parts' surfaces held |
// | `choose i`, `choose_none` | Names the literals for the next drags, or clears them |
// | `silhouette f c h n` | A facing's silhouette |
// | `fit f c h n` | Fits the named literals so the silhouette matches a reference image (`--reference`) |
// | `spec` | Runs the subject's spec: each check's value, target and miss, and how many checks hold |
// | `blueprint f` | Draws the blueprint's outline from the side, front or top (0 to 2) over that view, and says where the silhouette misses it |
// | `fit_blueprint f n` | Fits the named literals to the blueprint, as to a reference image |
//
// `look [--png file]` is the work loop in one command: it saves the contact sheet (`look.png`
// unless given), marks on a copy what changed since the last `look` (`<file>-changed.png`), and
// gives the diagnosis and the spec in brief. Warnings while the lens builds are shown as a
// count; `wrela check` shows them in full. `beside`, `variants` and `sweep` compare by eye
// (look.wrela).
//
// **How the lens solves.** A drag solves for the literals by least squares on the distance's
// derivatives (`std::lift::gradient`). It holds fixed points on the other parts' surfaces (those
// a part's share says the part doesn't decide), and checks the result on a 192³ grid before it
// accepts it: it takes back a step that would split the subject into pieces. The values end
// rounded to the literals' own decimals. A fit minimizes the difference between the silhouette
// and the reference with Levenberg–Marquardt, using each pixel's ray minimum, with the
// derivatives by the envelope theorem; it then rounds to decimals and reports the IoU.
//
// **The server** (`serve`, port 8417 unless `--port` is given) is `std::tool::serve`'s: it
// answers only requests addressed to this machine by name, and takes posts only from its own
// pages. It writes the lens's edits (a post to `studio/edit`) through `toolchain::edit` and gives
// a fit its reference (`studio/reference`). It watches the subject's files: a change to
// literals only goes to the open lens as new values; any other change rebuilds the lens, and the
// page reloads (server.wrela). Nothing of the studio is in a game's build.

use lens::{
    Built, Lens, Place, actions, build, call, cpu_action, invoke, last_json, logs, read_png,
    read_text, reference_mask, save_png, screen, start, typed,
}
use look::{Framing, Photo, changed, look_answer, own_framing, parse_registration, registered, sheet}
use json::{f32_text, obj, round3}
use std::collections::Vec
use std::input::Script
use std::io::print
use std::math::is_finite
use std::string::String
use std::tool::{ToolError, args}
use std::tool::drive
use std::tool::drive::Scalar
use std::tool::files
use std::tool::time
use std::tool::files::rooted
use toolkit::command::size_of

/// The root the tool reads the workspace in, and the root its output goes in.
pub const WS: Text = "ws"
pub const OUT: Text = "out"

/// The screen a headless run uses unless told: under 900 pixels wide, so the views fill it
/// (wider, the lens draws its panel for people beside them).
pub const SIZE: (u32, u32) = (896, 896)

const USAGE: Text = "usage: wrela tool studio -- <package-dir> [serve [--port N] | build | run <script> | look | beside <photo> | variants <package-dir>... | sweep <literal> <value>... | <action> [args...]] [--png FILE] [--view F] [--size WxH] [--reference PNG] [--debug]"

/// The command line, read: the positional words, and the flags.
pub struct Command: Clone {
    pub rest: Vec<String>,
    pub png: Option<String>,
    pub size: (u32, u32),
    pub port: u16,
    pub debug: bool,
    pub reference: Option<String>,
}

/// The command line `given`, or `None` for a usage error.
pub fn read_command(given: [String]) -> Option<Command> {
    var c = Command {
        rest: Vec::new(),
        png: None,
        size: SIZE,
        port: 8417,
        debug: false,
        reference: None,
    }
    var i = 0
    while i < given.len() {
        let a = given[i].as_str()
        if a == "--png" || a == "--size" || a == "--port" || a == "--reference" {
            if i + 1 >= given.len() {
                return None
            }
            let v = given[i + 1].as_str()
            if a == "--png" {
                c.png = Some(String::from(v))
            } else if a == "--reference" {
                c.reference = Some(String::from(v))
            } else if a == "--size" {
                c.size = size_of(v)?
            } else {
                let p = v.parse_u32()?
                if p > 65535 {
                    return None
                }
                c.port = u16(p)
            }
            i += 2
            continue
        }
        if a == "--debug" {
            c.debug = true
        } else if a.starts_with("--") && a != "--view" && a != "--registration" {
            // A flag this tool doesn't take, refused before anything is built.
            return None
        } else {
            c.rest.push(String::from(a))
        }
        i += 1
    }
    if c.rest.is_empty() {
        return None
    }
    Some(c)
}

/// One of the lens's actions, as the command line gives it: its export and the export's
/// arguments (by the lens's table), and for a move or a fit, the literals it may change.
pub struct Action: Clone {
    pub name: String,
    pub args: Vec<Scalar>,
    pub literals: Vec<Scalar>,
}

/// `name` and `args` read as one of `table`'s actions, or why not.
pub fn parse_action(
    table: [(String, String)],
    name: str,
    args: [String],
) -> Result<Action, String> {
    var kinds = String::new()
    var found = false
    for t in table {
        let (n, k) = t
        if n.as_str() == name {
            kinds = k.clone()
            found = true
        }
    }
    if !found {
        var names = String::new()
        for k in 0..table.len() {
            let (n, _) = table[k].clone()
            if k > 0 {
                names.push_str(", ")
            }
            names.push_str(n.as_str())
        }
        return Err(
            String::from(
                f"the lens has no action `{name}` (it has serve, build, run, {names.as_str()})",
            ),
        )
    }
    // A move's and a fit's arguments past their own name the literals they may change.
    let k = kinds.len()
    let named = if (name == "move" || name == "fit") && args.len() > k { args.len() - k } else { 0 }
    if args.len() != k + named {
        return Err(String::from(f"`{name}` takes {k} arguments, not {args.len()}"))
    }
    var literals: Vec<Scalar> = Vec::new()
    for i in k..args.len() {
        let Some(n) = args[i].as_str().parse_i32() else {
            return Err(String::from(f"`{args[i].as_str()}` isn't a literal's index"))
        }
        if n < 0 {
            return Err(String::from(f"`{args[i].as_str()}` isn't a literal's index"))
        }
        literals.push(Scalar::I32(n))
    }
    var values: Vec<Scalar> = Vec::new()
    for i in 0..k {
        let a = args[i].as_str()
        let v = if kinds.as_str().byte(i) == 117 {
            match a.parse_i32() {
                Some(n) => if n >= 0 { Some(Scalar::I32(n)) } else { None },
                None => None,
            }
        } else {
            match a.parse_f32() {
                Some(x) => if is_finite(x) { Some(Scalar::F32(x)) } else { None },
                None => None,
            }
        }
        let Some(v) = v else { return Err(String::from(f"`{a}` isn't a number")) }
        values.push(v)
    }
    Ok(Action { name: String::from(name), args: values, literals })
}

/// The tool: reads the command line, builds the lens, and does what it says.
pub fn tool() -> u32 {
    let Some(c) = read_command(args()) else {
        print(USAGE)
        return 2
    }
    let Some(subject) = rooted(WS, c.rest[0].as_str()) else {
        print(USAGE)
        return 2
    }
    let Some(out) = rooted(OUT, c.rest[0].as_str()) else {
        print(USAGE)
        return 2
    }
    let action = if c.rest.len() > 1 { c.rest[1].clone() } else { String::from("serve") }
    let place = Place {
        ws: String::from(WS),
        files: String::from(WS),
        outs: String::from(OUT),
        page: String::new(),
        subject: subject.clone(),
        out,
        overrides: Vec::new(),
        debug: c.debug,
    }
    run(take place, c, action.as_str(), c.rest[0].as_str())
}

/// What a command line (`c`) asks of the lens on the subject at `place` (named `shown` on the
/// command line): an exit status, after printing why if it failed.
pub fn run(place: take Place, c: Command, a: str, shown: str) -> u32 {
    // The words after the action: its arguments.
    var rest: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
    for k in 2..c.rest.len() {
        rest.push(c.rest[k].clone())
    }
    let commands = ["serve", "build", "look", "beside", "variants", "sweep", "run"]
    var command = false
    for k in commands {
        if a == k {
            command = true
        }
    }
    // A PNG's path is from the workspace's directory, and in it: one that isn't is refused
    // before anything is built.
    if let Some(png) = c.png.clone() {
        if rooted(place.files.as_str(), png.as_str()).is_none() {
            print(
                f"error: `{png.as_str()}` isn't a path in the workspace: a PNG goes in the workspace, by its path from the workspace's directory",
            )
            return 2
        }
    }
    // Refuse an invalid action before compiling the lens: trying an action name or correcting a
    // numeric argument mustn't cost a full build.
    var requested: Option<Action> = None
    if !command {
        var kind = glue::LensKind::Field
        if let Ok(Some(t)) = read_text(f"{place.subject.as_str()}/lens.wrela") {
            kind = glue::lens_kind(t.as_str())
        }
        match parse_action(actions(kind), a, rest) {
            Ok(p) => requested = Some(take p),
            Err(why) => {
                print(f"error: {why.as_str()}")
                return 2
            },
        }
    }
    var mask: Option<Vec<u8>> = None
    if let Some(r) = c.reference.clone() {
        let Some(path) = rooted(place.files.as_str(), r.as_str()) else {
            print(USAGE)
            return 2
        }
        match read_png(path.as_str()) {
            Ok(Some(image)) => {
                let (iw, ih, rgba) = image
                match reference_mask(iw, ih, rgba) {
                    Ok(m) => mask = Some(take m),
                    Err(why) => {
                        print(f"error: {why.as_str()}")
                        return 2
                    },
                }
            },
            Ok(None) => {
                print(f"error: can't read the reference {r.as_str()}: it isn't there")
                return 2
            },
            Err(why) => {
                print(f"error: can't read the reference {r.as_str()}: {why.message()}")
                return 2
            },
        }
    }
    // A served lens's builds are generations of this run's own, in `<out>/serve`: the last
    // run's go first.
    var at = place.clone()
    if a == "serve" {
        let Ok(date) = time::utc_now().wait() else { return 1 }
        let _ = files::remove_all(f"{place.out.as_str()}/serve").wait()
        at = server::serving_place(take at, f"{date.seconds}{date.nanos}")
    }
    let built = match build(take at) {
        Ok(x) => take x,
        Err(why) => {
            print(f"error: {why.message()}")
            return 1
        },
    }
    if !built.errors.is_empty() {
        print(built.errors.as_str())
        return 1
    }
    // Warnings in a line each time the lens builds would bury its answers: their count, and
    // where to read them.
    if built.warnings > 0 {
        let s = if built.warnings == 1 { "" } else { "s" }
        let them = if built.warnings == 1 { "it" } else { "them" }
        print(f"{built.warnings} warning{s}: `wrela check {shown}` shows {them}")
    }
    var result: Result<(), ToolError> = Ok(())
    if a == "build" {
        print(f"built the lens on `{shown}` in {built.page.as_str()}")
    } else if a == "serve" {
        result = server::run_server(place.clone(), built, c.port, take mask, shown)
    } else if a == "look" {
        let png = match c.png.clone() {
            Some(p) => take p,
            None => String::from("look.png"),
        }
        match look_cmd(built, place.out.as_str(), place.files.as_str(), png.as_str(), c.size) {
            Ok(answer) => print(answer.as_str()),
            Err(why) => result = Err(take why),
        }
    } else if a == "beside" || a == "variants" || a == "sweep" {
        match compare(place, built, a, rest, c) {
            Ok(answered) => {
                let (status, answer) = take answered
                if status != 0 {
                    print(USAGE)
                    return status
                }
                print(answer.as_str())
            },
            Err(why) => result = Err(take why),
        }
    } else if a == "run" {
        if c.rest.len() < 3 {
            print(USAGE)
            return 2
        }
        let Some(script) = rooted(place.files.as_str(), c.rest[2].as_str()) else {
            print(USAGE)
            return 2
        }
        let Ok(Some(lines)) = read_text(script.as_str()) else {
            print(f"error: can't read {c.rest[2].as_str()}")
            return 2
        }
        result = session(built, script.as_str(), lines.as_str(), c.size, take mask)
    } else {
        let Some(act) = take requested else { return 2 }
        let png = match c.png.clone() {
            Some(p) => rooted(place.files.as_str(), p.as_str()),
            None => None,
        }
        match one_action(built, act, c.size, take png, take mask) {
            Ok(lines) => print_all(lines),
            Err(why) => result = Err(take why),
        }
    }
    match take result {
        Ok(()) => 0,
        Err(why) => {
            print(f"error: {why.message()}")
            1
        },
    }
}

/// Prints each of `lines`.
fn print_all(lines: [String]) {
    for l in lines {
        print(l.as_str())
    }
}

/// `r`'s failure, a pure step's (`look`'s), as the tool's.
fn own<T>(r: take Result<T, String>) -> Result<T, ToolError> {
    (take r).map_err(|e| ToolError::new(e.as_str()))
}

/// One action: its literals chosen, its export called, the answer printed, and with `png` (a
/// root path), the screen after saved.
pub fn one_action(
    built: Built,
    a: Action,
    size: (u32, u32),
    png: take Option<String>,
    mask: take Option<Vec<u8>>,
) -> Result<Vec<String>, ToolError> {
    let (w, h) = size
    // These exports print their answer at once: the program's own action, without the GPU's
    // setup, its shaders' compiling and frames that only draw an unseen image.
    let cpu = png.is_none() && cpu_action(a.name.as_str()) && built.kind == glue::LensKind::Field
    var lens = start(built, w, h, cpu, take mask)?
    if cpu {
        let _ = invoke(mut lens, a.name.as_str(), a.args)?
    } else {
        for k in 0..a.literals.len() {
            let _ = invoke(mut lens, "choose", [a.literals[k]])?
        }
        call(mut lens, a.name.as_str(), a.args, deferred: false)?
    }
    let printed = logs(mut lens)
    if let Some(p) = take png {
        save_png(p.as_str(), w, h, screen(mut lens)?)?
    }
    Ok(printed)
}

/// A session: each line of `text` (the script at `script`, a root path) a command typed into the
/// lens (then Enter), or `png FILE` (the screen, saved, its path relative to the script's
/// directory), or `#` a comment.
pub fn session(
    built: Built,
    script: str,
    text: str,
    size: (u32, u32),
    mask: take Option<Vec<u8>>,
) -> Result<(), ToolError> {
    let (w, h) = size
    let parts = script.split("/")
    let (from, _) = parts[parts.len() - 1]
    let base = String::from(script.slice(0, from))
    var lens = start(built, w, h, cpu: false, reference: take mask)?
    let _ = logs(mut lens)
    let ranges = text.lines()
    for k in 0..ranges.len() {
        let (from, to) = ranges[k]
        let line = String::from(text.slice(from, to).trim())
        if line.is_empty() || line.as_str().starts_with("#") {
            continue
        }
        if line.as_str().starts_with("png ") {
            let file = String::from(f"{base.as_str()}{line.as_str().slice(4, line.len()).trim()}")
            lens::frames(mut lens, Script::frames())?
            save_png(file.as_str(), w, h, screen(mut lens)?)?
            continue
        }
        let at = lens.frame
        lens::frames(mut lens, typed(at, line.as_str()))?
        lens::settle(mut lens)?
        print_all(logs(mut lens))
    }
    Ok(())
}

/// `look`: the contact sheet saved (to `png`, from the workspace's directory), what changed
/// since the last look marked on a copy (`<png>-changed.png`), and the diagnosis and the spec,
/// in brief: one answer for the loop an author goes round.
pub fn look_cmd(
    built: Built,
    out: str,
    files: str,
    png: str,
    size: (u32, u32),
) -> Result<String, ToolError> {
    let (w, h) = size
    let Some(path) = rooted(files, png) else {
        return Err(ToolError::new(f"`{png}` isn't a path in the workspace"))
    }
    var lens = start(built, w, h, cpu: false, reference: None)?
    // The contact sheet, and the diagnosis's and the spec's answers (null if one isn't JSON).
    call(mut lens, "view", [Scalar::I32(4)], deferred: false)?
    let now = screen(mut lens)?
    save_png(path.as_str(), w, h, now.clone())?
    var answers: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
    for k in 0..2 {
        let name = if k == 0 { "diagnose" } else { "spec" }
        let args = if k == 0 {
            Vec::from([Scalar::F32(0.0), Scalar::F32(0.0), Scalar::F32(0.0), Scalar::F32(0.0)])
        } else { Vec::new() }
        call(mut lens, name, args, deferred: false)?
        answers.push(match last_json(logs(mut lens)) {
            Some(j) => take j,
            None => String::from("null"),
        })
    }
    // What changed since the last look.
    let last = String::from(f"{out}/last-look.png")
    var changed_json = String::from("null")
    if let Ok(Some(image)) = read_png(last.as_str()) {
        let (lw, lh, old) = image
        if lw == w && lh == h {
            let (marked, count) = changed(now, old)
            let end = if png.ends_with(".png") { png.len() - 4 } else { png.len() }
            let stem = png.slice(0, end)
            let marked_name = String::from(f"{stem}-changed.png")
            let Some(marked_path) = rooted(files, marked_name.as_str()) else {
                return Err(ToolError::new("no path"))
            }
            save_png(marked_path.as_str(), w, h, take marked)?
            changed_json = obj()
                .int("pixels", count)
                .text("png", marked_name.as_str())
                .num("share", round3(f64(count) / (f64(w) * f64(h))))
                .done()
        }
    }
    let _ = save_png(last.as_str(), w, h, take now)
    Ok(look_answer(png, changed_json.as_str(), answers[0].as_str(), answers[1].as_str()))
}

/// `beside <photo> [--registration g,m,z,faces]`, `variants <package>...` and `sweep <literal>
/// <value>...`, each with `[--view f]` and its PNG (`--png`, or `<action>.png`): 0, or 2 for a
/// usage error.
pub fn compare(
    place: Place,
    built: Built,
    action: str,
    args: [String],
    c: Command,
) -> Result<(u32, String), ToolError> {
    var facing = 0
    var plain: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
    var given_registration: Option<String> = None
    var i = 0
    while i < args.len() {
        if args[i].as_str() == "--registration" {
            if i + 1 >= args.len() || action != "beside" {
                return Ok((2, String::new()))
            }
            given_registration = Some(args[i + 1].clone())
            i += 2
            continue
        }
        if args[i].as_str() == "--view" {
            if i + 1 >= args.len() {
                return Ok((2, String::new()))
            }
            match args[i + 1].as_str().parse_u32() {
                Some(f) => if f < 4 { facing = f } else { return Ok((2, String::new())) },
                None => return Ok((2, String::new())),
            }
            i += 2
            continue
        }
        plain.push(args[i].clone())
        i += 1
    }
    let png = match c.png.clone() {
        Some(p) => take p,
        None => String::from(f"{action}.png"),
    }
    let Some(png_path) = rooted(place.files.as_str(), png.as_str()) else {
        return Ok((2, String::new()))
    }
    // Each panel is square: the screen's shorter side.
    let (sw, sh) = c.size
    let n = min(sw, sh)
    var lens = start(built, n, n, cpu: false, reference: None)?
    // The side framing the lens gives the subject (its `view` answer's first framing).
    call(mut lens, "view", [Scalar::I32(0)], deferred: true)?
    let view_answer = match last_json(logs(mut lens)) {
        Some(j) => take j,
        None => String::new(),
    }
    let own_frame = own(own_framing(view_answer.as_str()))?
    var panels: Vec<Vec<u8>> = Vec::new()
    var answer = String::new()
    if action == "beside" {
        if plain.len() != 1 {
            return Ok((2, String::new()))
        }
        let Some(photo_path) = rooted(place.files.as_str(), plain[0].as_str()) else {
            return Ok((2, String::new()))
        }
        let reg = match given_registration {
            Some(text) => own(parse_registration(text.as_str()))?,
            None => match registered(plain[0].as_str()) {
                Some(r) => r,
                None => return Err(
                    ToolError::new(
                        f"{plain[0].as_str()} has no registration: the references package registers its side photos (`references/<dir>/<name>.png` takes `<dir>/<name>.jpg`'s); give another photo's with `--registration ground_px,metres_per_px,z0_px,right|left`",
                    ),
                ),
            },
        }
        let shown = plain[0].clone()
        let image = match read_png(photo_path.as_str()) {
            Ok(Some(img)) => take img,
            _ => return Err(
                ToolError::new(
                    f"can't read the photo {shown.as_str()}: a photo is read as PNG (`sips -s format png photo.jpg --out {shown.as_str()}`)",
                ),
            ),
        }
        let (pw, ph, prgba) = take image
        let photo = Photo { r: reg, width: pw, height: ph, rgba: prgba }
        // Frame the subject and the photo's animal both: the subject's own framing's size, or
        // most of the photo's shorter side, whichever is larger.
        let photo_m = f32(min(pw, ph)) * reg.metres_per_px
        let half = max(own_frame.half, 0.45 * photo_m)
        let f = Framing { z: 0.0, y: half * 0.88, half }
        let shaded = shot(mut lens, [zoom_call(f), mode_call(0), view_call(0)])?
        let silhouette = shot(mut lens, [mode_call(4)])?
        let (left, over, covered, matched) = overlay(photo, f, n, silhouette)
        panels.push(take left)
        panels.push(take shaded)
        panels.push(take over)
        let share = if covered > 0 { round3(f64(matched) / f64(covered)) } else { 0.0 }
        let framing = obj()
            .raw("half", f32_text(f.half).as_str())
            .raw("y", f32_text(f.y).as_str())
            .raw("z", f32_text(f.z).as_str())
            .done()
        let listed = String::from(
            "[\"1: the photo, facing as the side view does\",\"2: your side view at the photo's scale\",\"3: the photo with your silhouette over it (tinted inside, red edge)\"]",
        )
        answer = obj()
            .text("action", "beside")
            .raw("framing", framing.as_str())
            .raw("metres_per_px_in_panels", f32_text(2.0 * f.half / (f32(n) / 2.0)).as_str())
            .raw("panels", listed.as_str())
            .text("png", png.as_str())
            .num("silhouette_on_dark_photo_pixels", share)
            .done()
    } else if action == "variants" {
        var legend = String::from("[")
        var dirs: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
        dirs.push(c.rest[0].clone())
        for k in 0..plain.len() {
            dirs.push(plain[k].clone())
        }
        for k in 0..dirs.len() {
            if k > 0 {
                // Each panel starts afresh: render before the next build, since a package can
                // be given twice.
                let Some(dir) = rooted(place.files.as_str(), dirs[k].as_str()) else {
                    return Ok((2, String::new()))
                }
                let Some(out) = rooted(place.outs.as_str(), dirs[k].as_str()) else {
                    return Ok((2, String::new()))
                }
                var other = place.clone()
                other.subject = take dir
                other.out = take out
                let next = build(take other)?
                if !next.errors.is_empty() {
                    print(next.errors.as_str())
                    return Err(ToolError::new(f"{dirs[k].as_str()} doesn't build"))
                }
                let _ = drive::close(lens.b).wait()
                lens = start(next, n, n, cpu: false, reference: None)?
            }
            var calls: Vec<(String, Vec<Scalar>)> = Vec::new()
            if facing == 0 {
                calls.push(zoom_call(own_frame))
            }
            calls.push(view_call(facing))
            panels.push(shot(mut lens, calls)?)
            if k > 0 {
                legend.push_str(",")
            }
            legend.push_str(
                obj().int("panel", k + 1).text("package", dirs[k].as_str()).done().as_str(),
            )
        }
        legend.push_str("]")
        answer = obj()
            .text("action", "variants")
            .raw("panels", legend.as_str())
            .text("png", png.as_str())
            .done()
    } else {
        if plain.len() < 1 {
            return Ok((2, String::new()))
        }
        let Some(literal) = plain[0].as_str().parse_i32() else { return Ok((2, String::new())) }
        if literal < 0 {
            return Ok((2, String::new()))
        }
        var values: Vec<f32> = Vec::new()
        for k in 1..plain.len() {
            let Some(v) = plain[k].as_str().parse_f32() else { return Ok((2, String::new())) }
            values.push(v)
        }
        var legend = String::from("[")
        for k in 0..values.len() {
            var calls: Vec<(String, Vec<Scalar>)> = Vec::new()
            calls.push(
                (String::from("set"), Vec::from([Scalar::I32(literal), Scalar::F32(values[k])])),
            )
            if facing == 0 {
                calls.push(zoom_call(own_frame))
            }
            calls.push(view_call(facing))
            panels.push(shot(mut lens, calls)?)
            if k > 0 {
                legend.push_str(",")
            }
            legend.push_str(
                obj()
                    .int("panel", k + 1)
                    .raw("value", f32_text(values[k]).as_str())
                    .done()
                    .as_str(),
            )
        }
        legend.push_str("]")
        answer = obj()
            .text("action", "sweep")
            .int("literal", u32(literal))
            .raw("panels", legend.as_str())
            .text("png", png.as_str())
            .done()
    }
    let (w, h, pixels) = sheet(panels, n)
    save_png(png_path.as_str(), w, h, take pixels)?
    Ok((0, answer))
}

fn zoom_call(f: Framing) -> (String, Vec<Scalar>) {
    (
        String::from("zoom"),
        Vec::from([Scalar::F32(0.0), Scalar::F32(f.y), Scalar::F32(f.z), Scalar::F32(f.half)]),
    )
}

fn view_call(facing: u32) -> (String, Vec<Scalar>) {
    (String::from("view"), Vec::from([Scalar::I32(i32(facing))]))
}

fn mode_call(mode: u32) -> (String, Vec<Scalar>) {
    (String::from("mode"), Vec::from([Scalar::I32(i32(mode)), Scalar::I32(0)]))
}

/// Runs `calls` and gives their final screen: consecutive field view controls need one image
/// after their last call; changes to the field and the actions that wait still settle.
pub fn shot(lens: mut Lens, calls: [(String, Vec<Scalar>)]) -> Result<Vec<u8>, ToolError> {
    for k in 0..calls.len() {
        borrow c = calls[k]
        call(mut lens, c.0.as_str(), c.1, k + 1 < calls.len())?
    }
    screen(mut lens)
}

/// `beside`'s photo panel and overlay: the photo (turned to face as the side view does) under
/// the framing `f`, `n` pixels square, and the photo with the subject's silhouette (`sil`, the
/// silhouette mode's screen) laid over it (inside tinted, its edge red); and how many pixels
/// the silhouette covers, and of those, how many are on the photo's dark pixels.
pub fn overlay(photo: Photo, f: Framing, n: u32, sil: [u8]) -> (Vec<u8>, Vec<u8>, u32, u32) {
    var left: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(n * n * 4)
    var over: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(n * n * 4)
    for _ in 0..n * n * 4 {
        left.push(0)
        over.push(0)
    }
    let inside = |i: u32| -> bool { sil[i] < 100 }
    var covered = 0
    var matched = 0
    for sy in 0..n {
        for sx in 0..n {
            let zy = f.point(f32(sx) + 0.5, f32(sy) + 0.5, f32(n))
            let c = photo.at(zy.x, zy.y)
            let i = (sy * n + sx) * 4
            left[i] = u8(c.x)
            left[i + 1] = u8(c.y)
            left[i + 2] = u8(c.z)
            left[i + 3] = 255
            var edge = false
            if inside(i) {
                for d in [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)] {
                    let (dx, dy) = d
                    let x2 = i32(sx) + dx
                    let y2 = i32(sy) + dy
                    if x2 < 0 ||
                        y2 < 0 ||
                        x2 >= i32(n) ||
                        y2 >= i32(n) ||
                        !inside((u32(y2) * n + u32(x2)) * 4) {
                        edge = true
                    }
                }
            }
            let tinted = if edge {
                vec3(230.0, 30.0, 30.0)
            } else if inside(i) {
                vec3(c.x * 0.6 + 60.0, c.y * 0.6 + 100.0, c.z * 0.6 + 40.0)
            } else {
                c
            }
            let t = clamp(tinted, vec3(0.0), vec3(255.0))
            over[i] = u8(t.x)
            over[i + 1] = u8(t.y)
            over[i + 2] = u8(t.z)
            over[i + 3] = 255
            if inside(i) {
                covered += 1
                if (c.x + c.y + c.z) / 3.0 < 175.0 {
                    matched += 1
                }
            }
        }
    }
    (left, over, covered, matched)
}

@test
fn action_arguments_fit_the_values_the_host_receives() {
    for value in ["2147483648", "4294967295", "-1"] {
        assert(
            parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "view", [String::from(value)]).is_err(),
            value,
        )
        var args: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
        for a in ["0", "0", "0", "0", "0", "0", value] {
            args.push(String::from(a))
        }
        assert(parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "move", args).is_err(), value)
    }
    for value in ["nan", "inf", "-inf", "1e99"] {
        var args: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
        for a in [value, "0", "0", "0"] {
            args.push(String::from(a))
        }
        assert(parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "zoom", args).is_err(), value)
    }
    assert(
        parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "view", [String::from("2147483647")]).is_ok(),
    )
    let Ok(m) = parse_action(
        actions(glue::LensKind::Field),
        "move",
        [
            String::from("0"),
            String::from("0"),
            String::from("0"),
            String::from("1"),
            String::from("1"),
            String::from("1"),
            String::from("4"),
        ],
    ) else {
        panic("a move naming a literal")
    }
    assert(m.args.len() == 6 && m.literals.len() == 1)
    let Err(no) = parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "no-such-action", []) else {
        panic("an action")
    }
    assert(
        no
            .as_str()
            .starts_with(
                "the lens has no action `no-such-action` (it has serve, build, run, view, zoom",
            ),
    )
    assert(
        parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Field), "probe", []).is_err() &&
            parse_action(actions(glue::LensKind::Map), "geology", [String::from("1")]).is_ok(),
    )
}

@test
fn the_command_line_reads_its_flags_and_paths_from_the_workspace() {
    var given: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
    for a in [
        "content/wolf/",
        "probe",
        "--size",
        "64x32",
        "1",
        "--png",
        "a.png",
        "0",
        "0",
        "--debug",
    ] {
        given.push(String::from(a))
    }
    let Some(c) = read_command(given) else { panic("a command") }
    assert(c.rest.len() == 5 && c.size == (64, 32) && c.debug)
    let Some(png) = c.png.clone() else { panic("a png") }
    assert(png.as_str() == "a.png")
    assert(rooted(WS, "content/wolf/") == Some(String::from("ws/content/wolf")))
    assert(rooted(WS, "./content/wolf") == Some(String::from("ws/content/wolf")))
    for bad in ["/tmp/x", "../x", "a//b", "a/./b", ""] {
        assert(rooted(WS, bad).is_none(), bad)
    }
    assert(read_command([String::from("x"), String::from("--size")]).is_none())
    assert(
        read_command(
            [String::from("x"), String::from("look"), String::from("--artifacts-only")],
        ).is_none(),
    )
    assert(size_of("0x5").is_none() && size_of("12").is_none())
}
